-- chem/volume.cub — the quantum volume at a four-valent vertex of a spin network, exactly. In loop quantum
-- gravity the volume of a region is an operator whose quanta sit at the vertices of the spin network
-- (Rovelli–Smolin 1995; Ashtekar–Lewandowski 1998); its square at a vertex v is
--   Q_v = Z · Σ_{I<J<K} ε(e_I, e_J, e_K) q_IJK,   q_IJK = ε_ijk X^i_I X^j_J X^k_K,   Z = i/4
-- (Brunnemann–Thiemann, "Simplification of the spectral analysis of the volume operator in loop quantum
-- gravity", Class. Quantum Grav. 23 (2006) 1289, gr-qc/0405060, eqs. 4, 9). At a gauge-invariant four-valent
-- vertex, closure J_4 = −(J_1 + J_2 + J_3) makes every q_IJK ± q_123, and Q_v = 2Z q_123 for their edge
-- orientation (eqs. 64–66). In the recoupling basis |j12⟩, max(|j1−j2|, |j3−j4|) ≤ j12 ≤ min(j1+j2, j3+j4)
-- (eq. 68), q_123 is tridiagonal with zero diagonal and i times antisymmetric, its one nonzero entry per
-- step (eq. 61):
--   ⟨a|q_123|a−1⟩ = [(j1+j2+a+1)(−j1+j2+a)(j1−j2+a)(j1+j2−a+1)]^½ [(j3+j4+a+1)(−j3+j4+a)(j3−j4+a)(j3+j4−a+1)]^½
--                   / √((2a−1)(2a+1)),   = −⟨a−1|q_123|a⟩.
-- Every such entry is the square root of a rational, and the characteristic polynomial of a Hermitian
-- tridiagonal matrix with zero diagonal obeys the three-term recurrence p_k = λ p_{k−1} − |b_k|² p_{k−2}, so
-- it has rational coefficients: the spectrum of q_123, and with it the vertex's volume (V_v = √|Q_v|), is
-- the roots of a polynomial computed here exactly, with no real number formed. Spins are doubled
-- (J = 2j, A = 2a) so that every quantity is a natural or a rational.
import "charge.cub"

